course: dictionary
lesson: 15431
title: Starvation: serious and silly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Starvation means serious suffering or death caused by having little or no food for a long time. «Many families faced starvation after the crops failed.» The clues are the crops failing and the families having little to eat, so this is a serious meaning, not just a tummy rumble.
explain: Starvation can also be a joke. «I'm dying of starvation!» said Sam, before tea. Sam is not really starving, because he is only a bit hungry. The word is exaggerated, which means made bigger than the truth. Ask yourself: is this serious, or is someone joking? The rest of the sentence tells you.
explain: Some phrases use starvation in a special way. «Starvation wages» means very low pay, so a worker can barely afford food. The word wages tells you it is about money for work, and starvation shows how small that money is.
fact: Starvation is usually uncountable, so you say «starvation», not «starvations».
fact: «Starvation» means serious suffering or death caused by having little or no food for a long time.
fact: In a famine, many people face starvation because there is not enough food for everyone.
fact: The Irish Great Famine (1845–1852) and the Holodomor in Ukraine (1932–1933) were times of terrible starvation.
fact: Aid groups bring food to people facing starvation, and in science, a body with no food uses up its fat first, then its muscle.
exercise: «Many families faced starvation after the crops failed.» What does starvation mean here? | A big, happy party | A new kind of farm tool | Feeling a bit peckish before dinner | *Serious suffering from having little or no food for a long time
exercise: Sam says, «I'm dying of starvation!» before tea. What does the joke show? | *He is exaggerating, because he is only a bit hungry | He has not eaten for a whole week | He is a doctor checking hunger | He is about to become ill
exercise: What does the phrase «starvation wages» mean? | *Very low pay | Pay given in gold coins | Very high pay | Pay given in food
test: «The town was under siege, and people faced starvation.» What does starvation mean in this sentence? | *Serious suffering or death from having little or no food | A party with lots of food | A funny joke about being hungry | A short holiday by the sea
test: Which phrase uses starvation to mean very low pay? | a famine in the past | *starvation wages | aid groups bring food | die of starvation
exam: Is «I'm dying of starvation!» said before tea a serious use or a joke? | *A joke, exaggerated | A serious famine report | A history lesson about a war | A medical fact about the body
